,'uraian','Explain the characteristics and generic structure of a report text! and then what is differences between report text and discriptive text!','','','','','','','Characteristics of Report Text:\r\nGeneral information\r\nIt explains something in general, such as animals, plants, places, or natural phenomena.\r\nUses factual information\r\nThe text is based on facts, not opinions or imagination.\r\nUses Simple Present Tense\r\nBecause it describes general truths or habits.\r\nUses technical or scientific terms\r\nEspecially in scientific topics.\r\nObjective\r\nThe writer does not include personal feelings.\r\nGeneric Structure of Report Text\r\n1. General Classification\r\n\r\nIntroduces the topic and gives general information about it.\r\n\r\n2. Description\r\n\r\nDescribes the characteristics, parts, habits, functions, or qualities of the topic.\r\n\r\nDifferences Between Report Text and Descriptive Text\r\nReport Text	Descriptive Text\r\nDescribes something in general	Describes a specific thing\r\nGives factual and scientific information	Gives detailed description of one object\r\nUses general participants	Uses specific participants\r\nObjective	Can be subjective\r\nExample: “Cats are mammals.”	Example: “My cat is very cute.”\r\nExample:\r\nReport Text:\r\n“Elephants are large mammals that live in Africa and Asia.”\r\nDescriptive Text:\r\n“My elephant at the zoo has big ears and long tusks.”'),(31917,'671',42,'PAT_9368','uraian','Write a short recount text about your unforgettable experience (minimum 8 sentences)!','','','','','','','Contoh Jawaban Recount Text:\r\n\r\nLast holiday, I went to my grandmother’s house. I went there with my family by car. We arrived in the afternoon. My grandmother cooked delicious food for us. The next day, we visited a beautiful beach near her house. We took many pictures there. I felt very happy during the holiday. Finally, we returned home on Sunday.'),(31918,'671',43,'PAT_9368','uraian','Arrange the following words into a good sentence!<div><br></div><div>“yesterday – cleaned – the students – classroom – the”</div>','','','','','','','“The students cleaned the classroom yesterday.”'),(31919,'671',44,'PAT_9368','uraian','Arrange the following sentences into a good procedure text!<div><br></div><div>Pour hot water into the cup.</div><div>Prepare a cup and a tea bag.</div><div>Serve the tea.</div><div>Put the tea bag into the cup.</div>','','','','','','','2 → 4 → 1 → 3'),(31920,'671',45,'PAT_9368','uraian','What is the difference between narrative text and recount text? Explain briefly!','','','','','','','Narrative Text bertujuan menghibur pembaca dan biasanya berisi cerita khayal atau legenda.\r\nRecount Text bertujuan menceritakan kembali pengalaman atau kejadian nyata di masa lalu.'),(31921,'675',1,'PAT_9372','pg','<b>Read the text carefully!</b><div><br></div><div>Dolphins are intelligent sea mammals. They live in oceans and seas around the world. Dolphins breathe through a blowhole on the top of their heads. They eat fish and squid. A dolphin can swim up to 60 kilometers per hour. Dolphins usually live in groups called pods.</div><div><br></div><div><b>What is the main idea of the text?</b></div>','<div>Dolphins are intelligent sea mammals</div><div>\r\n</div>','<div>Dolphins only live in rivers</div>','Dolphins are dangerous animals','<div>Dolphins cannot swim fast</div>','<div>Dolphins eat plants</div>','','A'),(31922,'675',2,'PAT_9372','pg','<b>Read the text carefully!</b><div><br></div><div>Dolphins are intelligent sea mammals. They live in oceans and seas around the world. Dolphins breathe through a blowhole on the top of their heads. They eat fish and squid. A dolphin can swim up to 60 kilometers per hour. Dolphins usually live in groups called pods.</div><div><br></div><div><b>Where do dolphins live?</b></div>','<div>In forests</div><div>\r\n</div><div>\r\n</div>','<div>In deserts</div>','<div>In mountains</div>','<div>In rivers only</div>','In oceans and seas','','E'),(3