pg','My brother ____ football every Sunday.','<div>play</div><div>\r\n</div><div>\r\n</div>','<div>played</div>','<div>plays</div>','<div>playing</div>','<div>played</div>','','C'),(32096,'672',40,'PAT_9369','pg','The students ____ English in the classroom every day.','<div>study</div><div>\r\n</div><div>\r\n</div>','<div>studied</div>','<div>studies</div>','<div>studying</div>','<div>to study</div>','','A'),(32097,'672',41,'PAT_9369','uraian','Explain the characteristics and generic structure of a report text! and then what is differences between report text and discriptive text!','','','','','','','Characteristics of Report Text:\r\nGeneral information\r\nIt explains something in general, such as animals, plants, places, or natural phenomena.\r\nUses factual information\r\nThe text is based on facts, not opinions or imagination.\r\nUses Simple Present Tense\r\nBecause it describes general truths or habits.\r\nUses technical or scientific terms\r\nEspecially in scientific topics.\r\nObjective\r\nThe writer does not include personal feelings.\r\nGeneric Structure of Report Text\r\n1. General Classification\r\n\r\nIntroduces the topic and gives general information about it.\r\n\r\n2. Description\r\n\r\nDescribes the characteristics, parts, habits, functions, or qualities of the topic.\r\n\r\nDifferences Between Report Text and Descriptive Text\r\nReport Text	Descriptive Text\r\nDescribes something in general	Describes a specific thing\r\nGives factual and scientific information	Gives detailed description of one object\r\nUses general participants	Uses specific participants\r\nObjective	Can be subjective\r\nExample: “Cats are mammals.”	Example: “My cat is very cute.”\r\nExample:\r\nReport Text:\r\n“Elephants are large mammals that live in Africa and Asia.”\r\nDescriptive Text:\r\n“My elephant at the zoo has big ears and long tusks.”'),(32098,'672',42,'PAT_9369','uraian','Write a short recount text about your unforgettable experience (minimum 8 sentences)!','','','','','','','Contoh Jawaban Recount Text:\r\n\r\nLast holiday, I went to my grandmother’s house. I went there with my family by car. We arrived in the afternoon. My grandmother cooked delicious food for us. The next day, we visited a beautiful beach near her house. We took many pictures there. I felt very happy during the holiday. Finally, we returned home on Sunday.'),(32099,'672',43,'PAT_9369','uraian','Arrange the following words into a good sentence!<div><br></div><div>“yesterday – cleaned – the students – classroom – the”</div>','','','','','','','“The students cleaned the classroom yesterday.”'),(32100,'672',44,'PAT_9369','uraian','Arrange the following sentences into a good procedure text!<div><br></div><div>Pour hot water into the cup.</div><div>Prepare a cup and a tea bag.</div><div>Serve the tea.</div><div>Put the tea bag into the cup.</div>','','','','','','','2 → 4 → 1 → 3'),(32101,'672',45,'PAT_9369','uraian','What is the difference between narrative text and recount text? Explain briefly!','','','','','','','Narrative Text bertujuan menghibur pembaca dan biasanya berisi cerita khayal atau legenda.\r\nRecount Text bertujuan menceritakan kembali pengalaman atau kejadian nyata di masa lalu.'),(32102,'821',6,'PAT_9515','pg','<p>Graffiti: Art or Problem?</p><p>\r\n<div>Graffiti is common in many cities today. Some people think graffiti is art, but others think it is a problem. I believe graffiti on public places without permission should be banned.\r\n</div><div>First, graffiti makes public places look dirty and damaged. Cleaning it also costs money. Second, too much graffiti can make people feel uncomfortable because the area looks unsafe. However, graffiti can be positive if it is made legally in special areas for artists.\r\n</div><div>In conclusion, graffiti without permission should not be allowed, but legal graffiti can still be appreciated as art.\r\n</div><div><br></div><div>What is the function of the sentence “However, graffiti can be positive…”?</div></p>','To introduce the thesis','To give a counterargument','To repeat the conclusion<div><br></div>','To explain the definition','To give statistics','','B'),(32103,'821',7,'PAT_9515','pg','<p>Graffiti: Art or Problem?</p><p>\r\n<div>Graffiti is common in many cities today. Some people think graffiti is art, but others think it is a problem. I believe graffiti on public places without permission should be banned.\r\n</div><div>First, graffiti makes public places look dirty and damaged. Cleaning it also costs money. Second, too much graffiti can make people feel uncomfortable because the area looks unsafe. However, graffiti can be positive if it is made legally in special areas for artists.\r\n</div><div>In conclusion, graffiti without permission should not be allowed, but legal graffiti can still be appreciated as art.\r\n</div><div><br></div><div>If a city provides special walls for graffiti artists, the writer would most likely…</div></p>','disagree strongly','support the idea','ignore the policy<div><br></div>','think graffiti should still be banned','believe it will fail','','B'),(32105,'783',26,'PAT_9243','pg','<p>“Bu Guru ngendika supaya para siswa aja mung seneng nyangkruk nganti lali sinau.”</p><p>Tembung “nyangkruk” kalebu tembung plutan saka tembung …</p>','cangkruk','ancuk','jangkruk','sangkruk','congkruk','','A'),(32106,'783',27,'PAT_9243','pg','<p>“Bocah-bocah padha nglumpuk ing balai desa kanggo latihan karawitan.”</p><p>Tembung “nglumpuk” asalé saka tembung …</p>','lumpuk','Ngelumpuk','klumpuk','ngumpuk','kumpulan','','B'),(32107,'783',28,'PAT_9243','pg','<p>“Nalika kerja bakti, warga padha teka kanthi semangat lan langsung nyiapke peralatan sing dibutuhake.”</p><p>Panganggone tembung plutan “nyiapke” ing ukara kasebut nduweni tujuan supaya …</p>','ukara luwih angel dimangerteni','basa dadi luwih resmi','pangucapan luwih praktis lan lumrah digunakake','ukara dadi luwih dawa','basa dadi kurang sopan','','C'),(32108,'783',29,'PAT_9243','pg','Tembung pl